  "title": "Sensorimotor contingency",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "6a714653-06cf-4cb2-a97f-2de5d9ed263b",
      "text": "A sensorimotor contingency is a law describing how sensory stimulation changes as a result of movement of the perceiver or of the thing perceived. What differentiates vision from audition or touch is the structure of these rules.",
